"DG_H2_02_desc" => 'I participated in the competition for the creation of the <span>new corporate image of PIMECAVA</span>, the Association of Cava Producers and Producers of Catalonia.<br>My goal was to design a <span>logo and visual identity</span> that captured the essence of the Catalan wine tradition and, at the same time, transmitted the modernity and dynamism of the sector.<br>My proposal was selected as a <span>finalist</span> of the competition, a milestone that recognized the <span>conceptual quality and innovative design</span> of the graphic solution presented to represent this important association of winemakers.',
"DG_H2_03_desc" => 'During the pandemic period in 2020, I led the design of all <span>graphic material for Clickedu\'s social media (Instagram and Twitter).<br>This project focused on <span>supporting and adding value to the education sector</span> at a time of critical transition to teleworking and distance learning.<br>I created a constant flow of <span>educational content, quick tutorials and messages of encouragement</span> for teachers. The goal was to make the Clickedu platform perceived as an <span>essential and accessible tool</span>, reinforcing its leadership and social commitment through visually clear and empathetic communication.',
"DG_H2_04_desc" => 'I developed the <span>full corporate image</span> for the <span>Coffeing</span> café in Barcelona, ​​seeking an aesthetic that reflected the quality of its product and the welcoming atmosphere.<br>The project began with the creation of the <span>logo</span>, establishing a modern and memorable visual identity. This was applied consistently across all brand material.<br>I designed the <span>business cards</span> and the <span>menus</span> (both for the food and wine offerings). I focused on ensuring a <span>clear hierarchy</span> of information and a <span>legible typography</span>, transforming each piece into an element that reinforces the customer experience.',
"DG_H2_05_desc" => 'I designed and created a key <span>commercial brochure</span> for the Clickedu sales department. The goal was to condense the platform\'s value proposition into a high-impact physical format.<br>The design was structured into three distinct sections: <span>Clickedu\'s Philosophy and Vision</span>, <span>Main features</span> of the platform and its benefits, and <span>Testimonials and opinions</span> from real customers, to generate trust and credibility.<br>This material was created to be a visual and concise support tool, facilitating the understanding and promotion of the educational solution in meetings and presentations.',
"DG_H2_06_desc" => 'As a graphic designer, I managed and created all <span>corporate and promotional material</span> for Clickedu, with the aim of reinforcing its brand image and supporting commercial strategies.<br>The project included the complete design of informative <span>catalogs</span> (paper and digital versions), <span>material for fairs and events</span> (roll-ups, banners, flyers and displays), and <span>various promotional material</span> (merchandising).<br>I was in charge of the layout, the selection of images and the adaptation of the visual identity to all media to guarantee <span>clear, coherent and professional communication</span> at all points of contact with the customer.',
"DG_H2_07_desc" => 'As a graphic designer at Clickedu, I created the <span>master sales presentation</span> (PowerPoint format) for the sales team.<br>This visual tool was strategically designed to structure the sales pitch and <span>clearly highlight the virtues and advantages</span> of the platform.<br>I focused on <span>data visualization</span> and a clean layout to explain the solutions that Clickedu offers to the complex <span>management of school centers</span>. The presentation became a key support to demonstrate the added value of the platform to potential customers, facilitating the sales task.',
"DG_H2_08_desc" => 'I participated in the packaging design of the <span>PowerG</span> brand\'s tool line, collaborating closely with the <span>ANIMA Design</span> studio in Barcelona.<br>The project consisted of creating packaging that was not only <span>functional and protective</span>, but also conveyed the <span>quality, robustness and professionalism</span> of the tools.<br>I was in charge of the graphic structuring. We implemented a modern and clear industrial aesthetic, ensuring brand coherence across the entire product range.',
"DG_H2_10_desc" => 'Development of the complete visual identity for Babou, a brand specializing in handmade baby supplies and DIY crafts. The project included creating the logo, brand identity, and professional business cards, reflecting the warmth and quality of their products. Our strategy focused on social media presence and Instagram content, generating an engaging visual style that drives engagement and online sales. Babou\'s branding now directly connects with its target audience of crafts and personalized gifts.',

